      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOPE DE LUNA (4) comes here with a fitness edge over most of these in a very thin contest. Loomed strongly with the 59kg when an improved second over 1400m at Tamworth. Well drawn again and looks hard to hold out. A LITTLE BIT DUSTY (9) started ($1.26 fav) on debut with a fighting on speed second over 1000m at Muswellbrook. Will appreciate the extra ground and looks to have genuine top three prospects. AKUMA (1) covered plenty of ground from the wide gate with a tiring seventh over 1400m at Tamworth. Gets a better set-up for this with the 2kg claimer. Worth thought.IRISH ACCOLADE (3) backs-up quickly and gets a better set-up for this with the claim. Went back from the draw and failed to get into the contest when tenth over 1615m at Taree. Place best.",
